commit dc4a7ed33b4167167649ad08343887ac39dde242
Author: Nate Ferrell <nate@scrthq.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 15 21:41:01 2026 -0500

    fix(sync): a server counter past the last event no longer pulls the run every two seconds

    An undo takes an event out of a session log and leaves the session
    counter where it was, so the server legitimately says seq 8 while the
    last event it holds is 7. The engine read that gap as somebody else
    having moved: it fetched, got no events but a fresh members list, took
    the new object for news, saved the run and told the app a run had
    arrived. The page answered by reloading the log and dropping whatever
    block was in flight, so a roll at the first step could never be
    answered.

    The device now remembers the counter it has caught up to, in the run
    record's own seq, and asks again only once the manifest moves past it.
    What the record carries besides its log is compared by value, so a
    fresh members list saying the old thing is not news. And the page
    leaves its log, and the block in flight, alone when the pulled log
    holds the same events.

    The pack plan had its own version of the same loop: the server keeps a
    tombstone for a pack deleted anywhere, and a device that purged its own
    copy passes ago has nothing left to forget, so every pass sent a delete
    to storage for a row already gone and told the app a pack had arrived.

